<title>USA: Turkey seeks $125 mln in support for F-16 jets.</title>
<headline>Turkey seeks $125 mln in support for F-16 jets.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Pentagon said that the government of Turkey was seeking authorization for $125 million in logistical support from several defense firms for its fleet of F-16 jet fighters.</p>
<p>In a notification to Congress, the Defense Department said the Clinton administration intended to approve the request.</p>
<p>The chief U.S. defense contractors would be Lockheed Martin Corp, the aircraft engine division of General Electric Co, the guidance and control systems division of Litton Industries, and Westinghouse Electric.</p>
</text>
